course: dictionary
lesson: 6011
title: A word for a helper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mediator is a person who helps two people or groups who disagree to talk calmly and reach an agreement. The clues are in the words around it: a mediator helps, and their job is to make people agree.
explain: «If parents cannot agree, a mediator (a trained helper who helps them agree) or a family court helps decide what is best for the children.» The bracket explains the word for you. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "a trained helper who helps them agree" fits, so you have it right.
explain: A good mediator is neutral, which means fair and not on either side. They do not pick a winner. They help both sides listen, speak calmly and find a way forward that both can accept.
fact: A mediator is a neutral helper who does not take sides.
fact: «Peer mediators» are pupils who are trained to help classmates sort out playground quarrels.
fact: In law, a mediator can help parents, families or workers settle an argument without going to court.
fact: Mediator is a noun: one mediator, two mediators.
fact: In church teaching, Christians believe that Jesus is the mediator between God and people.
exercise: «In school, some pupils are trained as peer mediators.» What is a peer mediator? | A pupil who starts most of the quarrels | A teacher who gives out homework | A pupil who always arrives late | *A pupil trained to help classmates sort out quarrels
exercise: Maya and Sam keep arguing about the football. A friend helps them talk calmly until they agree. What job is the friend doing? | Telling the teacher who is right | *Acting as a mediator | Running the fastest race | Taking the ball away
exercise: What does a neutral mediator do? | Takes sides with whoever shouts loudest | Decides to win the argument for themselves | Leaves the room so nobody can talk | *Stays fair and does not take sides
test: Which situation needs a mediator? | The class walks to the park | A child reads a book quietly by the window | *Two friends have fallen out and want help to make up | Someone is baking a birthday cake
test: «Jesus is the mediator between God and people.» Based on the lesson, what does this sentence suggest? | *Jesus helps God and people come together | Jesus never speaks to people | Jesus is a teacher of maths | Jesus is a person who causes quarrels
exam: Which best describes a mediator? | Someone who never says anything at all | Someone who writes letters to the newspaper | *Someone who helps two sides talk calmly and reach an agreement | Someone who takes sides and wins the argument
